<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transport From Delhi To Gorakhpur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a vehicle reaches its destination, a thorough handover process ensures that the car’s condition matches the expectations set at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The delivery handover focuses on three critical checks: a daylight condition re‑inspection compared with the original pickup photos, verification of the odometer reading against the load‑receipt (LR) bilty, and a final signed condition sign‑off by both parties.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Conduct the inspection in natural daylight to reveal any surface imperfections, dents, or scratches that may be hidden under artificial lighting.</li>
      <li>Use the pickup photographs as a baseline. Compare each exterior panel, glass surface, and interior area side‑by‑side with the images taken at origin.</li>
      <li>Document any discrepancies with timestamped photos and notes, highlighting the exact location and nature of the damage.</li>
      <li>If the vehicle passes the visual comparison, mark the item as “Verified – No New Damage” on the handover checklist.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Locate the odometer reading displayed on the vehicle’s instrument cluster.</li>
      <li>Reference the LR bilty, which records the mileage at the time of loading. The LR bilty should be signed by the carrier and the shipper.</li>
      <li>Confirm that the current reading is equal to or greater than the mileage on the bilty; any unexpected increase may indicate unauthorized travel.</li>
      <li>Record the verified odometer value on the handover form, noting any variance and the reason (e.g., detour, test drive).</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Both the carrier’s representative and the receiver review the inspection findings together.</li>
      <li>Each party signs the condition report, acknowledging that the vehicle’s state matches the documented evidence.</li>
      <li>The signed document becomes the final legal record; retain a copy for the carrier’s files and provide the receiver with an original.</li>
      <li>Any unresolved issues must be noted in the “Exceptions” section before signatures are affixed.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>Completing these steps ensures transparency, protects both the shipper and receiver from disputes, and maintains the integrity of the logistics chain for automobile and car shipments.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



